# Special relativity's Lorentz boosts and their one-parameter group, modeled by the kernel through RAPIDITY. A Lorentz
# boost mixes the time direction with one space direction, carrying one inertial frame into another moving at constant
# velocity. The natural parameter of a boost is not the velocity v but the RAPIDITY phi, the hyperbolic angle, related by
# v = tanh(phi) in units of the speed of light. The boost is a HYPERBOLIC ROTATION through this angle: time and space mix
# by cosh(phi) and sinh(phi) exactly as a circular rotation mixes by cosine and sine. The decisive fact is the COMPOSITION
# LAW. Two boosts in the same direction compose by ADDING their rapidities, boost(phi1) then boost(phi2) = boost(phi1 +
# phi2), even though the corresponding velocities add by the relativistic formula and never reach the speed of light. So
# the rapidity is the additive coordinate behind the bounded, sub-luminal velocity, and the boosts form a ONE-PARAMETER
# ABELIAN GROUP isomorphic to the additive integers. This file models that group exactly. A boost carries a signed integer
# rapidity (reusing the rung from the integer file), composition adds the rapidities, the zero-rapidity boost is the
# identity, and the negated-rapidity boost is the inverse. The kernel proves the four group axioms, associativity,
# identity, inverse, and commutativity, each delegated to the proven integer addition group. A boost preserves the
# Minkowski INTERVAL s^2 = t^2 - x^2, whose SIGN classifies every event as timelike (inside the light cone), lightlike
# (on it), or spacelike (outside). This classification is LORENTZ INVARIANT: a boost carries timelike to timelike,
# spacelike to spacelike, and fixes the LIGHT CONE itself, the lightlike events where t = x. The light cone being boost
# invariant is the geometric statement that the speed of light is the same in every inertial frame.

load @cluesurf/form/code/number/integer
  find rung
  find combine
  find negate
  find combine-zero-right-is-self
  find combine-zero-left-is-self
  find combine-is-associative
  find combine-is-commutative
  find combine-negate-right-is-zero

# A Lorentz BOOST in a fixed direction, carrying its RAPIDITY as a signed integer. The rapidity is the additive hyperbolic
# angle phi with v = tanh(phi). Distinct rapidities are distinct boosts, and every signed integer names one boost, so the
# boosts are in exact correspondence with the rung, the additive integers.
form boost
  link rapidity, like rung

# COMPOSE two boosts: apply one then the other and ADD their rapidities. This is the group law of the boost group. The
# velocities do not add this simply (they obey the relativistic sum and stay below the speed of light), but the rapidities
# add freely, which is the whole reason rapidity is the right coordinate.
task compose
  take first, like boost
  take next, like boost
  like boost
  fork case, read first
    case boost
      link first-rapidity, name rapidity
      fork case, read next
        case boost
          link next-rapidity, name rapidity
          send back
            make boost
              bind rapidity
                call combine
                  read first-rapidity
                  read next-rapidity

# The IDENTITY boost: zero rapidity, hence zero velocity, the frame at rest relative to itself. It is the neutral element
# of the boost group.
task identity-boost
  like boost
  send back
    make boost
      bind rapidity
        make zero-int

# The INVERSE boost: negate the rapidity, the boost of the same magnitude in the opposite direction. Composing a boost with
# its inverse returns to rest.
task inverse-boost
  take b, like boost
  like boost
  fork case, read b
    case boost
      link rapidity
      send back
        make boost
          bind rapidity
            call negate
              read rapidity

# Read the rapidity out of a boost, the signed integer hyperbolic angle it carries.
task rapidity-of
  take b, like boost
  like rung
  fork case, read b
    case boost
      link rapidity
      send back
        read rapidity

# COMPOSING WITH THE IDENTITY ON THE RIGHT IS THE BOOST ITSELF: compose b identity = b. The zero-rapidity boost leaves any
# boost unchanged. Proved by unfolding to integer addition with zero on the right, which the integer file proves is the
# identity.
rule compose-identity-right-is-self
  mark b, like boost
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compose
        read b
        call identity-boost
      read b
  fold b
    cite combine-zero-right-is-self

# COMPOSING WITH THE IDENTITY ON THE LEFT IS THE BOOST ITSELF: compose identity b = b. The mirror, by zero on the left.
rule compose-identity-left-is-self
  mark b, like boost
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compose
        call identity-boost
        read b
      read b
  fold b
    cite combine-zero-left-is-self

# COMPOSITION IS ASSOCIATIVE: compose (compose a b) c = compose a (compose b c). The grouping of three successive boosts
# does not matter. Proved by unfolding each composition to integer addition and citing the proven associativity of the
# integers.
rule compose-is-associative
  mark a, like boost
  mark b, like boost
  mark c, like boost
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compose
        call compose
          read a
          read b
        read c
      call compose
        read a
        call compose
          read b
          read c
  fold a, b, c
    cite combine-is-associative

# COMPOSITION IS COMMUTATIVE: compose a b = compose b a. Boosts in the same direction commute, the abelian one-parameter
# subgroup of the Lorentz group. This is exactly the commutativity of rapidity addition, delegated to the integers. (Boosts
# in DIFFERENT directions do not commute; their failure to commute is the Thomas rotation. This file models the single
# direction, the abelian line.)
rule compose-is-commutative
  mark a, like boost
  mark b, like boost
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compose
        read a
        read b
      call compose
        read b
        read a
  fold a, b
    cite combine-is-commutative

# THE INVERSE BOOST CANCELS: compose b (inverse-boost b) = identity. A boost followed by its opposite returns to rest, the
# additive inverse of the rapidity. With identity, associativity, and commutativity, the boosts are an ABELIAN GROUP under
# composition, the one-parameter group of Lorentz boosts in a fixed direction. Proved by unfolding to integer addition of
# a rapidity and its negation, which the integer file proves is zero.
rule compose-inverse-right-is-identity
  mark b, like boost
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compose
        read b
        call inverse-boost
          read b
      call identity-boost
  fold b
    cite combine-negate-right-is-zero

# --- The Minkowski interval, the light cone, and Lorentz invariance of the causal classification. ---

# The causal CLASS of an event, the sign of its Minkowski interval s^2 = t^2 - x^2. TIMELIKE (s^2 positive) events lie
# inside the light cone and can be connected by a slower-than-light worldline; LIGHTLIKE (s^2 zero) events lie exactly on
# the light cone, connected only by a light ray; SPACELIKE (s^2 negative) events lie outside, with no causal connection.
# This three-way class is the Lorentz-invariant content of an event's separation from the origin.
form interval-class
  case timelike
  case lightlike
  case spacelike

# An EVENT as a discrete light-cone coordinate: a time step and a space step, each a signed integer count of unit cells.
# The interval is t^2 - x^2, and its sign is what classifies the event.
form event
  link time, like rung
  link space, like rung

# Compare two natural magnitudes and report the interval class from the sign of (time magnitude) minus (space magnitude):
# bigger time is timelike, equal is lightlike, bigger space is spacelike. This is t^2 - x^2 reduced to |t| versus |x|.
task class-from-magnitudes
  take time-magnitude, like natural
  take space-magnitude, like natural
  like interval-class
  fork case, read time-magnitude
    case zero
      fork case, read space-magnitude
        case zero
          send back
            make lightlike
        case succ
          send back
            make spacelike
    case succ
      link time-prior, name prior
      fork case, read space-magnitude
        case zero
          send back
            make timelike
        case succ
          link space-prior, name prior
          send back
            call class-from-magnitudes
              read time-prior
              read space-prior

# The unsigned MAGNITUDE of a rung: drop the sign, keeping the count. A negative -(p+1) and a positive p+1 both have
# magnitude p+1, and zero has magnitude zero. Squaring an interval coordinate erases its sign, so only the magnitude
# matters to the interval class.
task magnitude-of
  take z, like rung
  like natural
  fork case, read z
    case negsucc
      link prior
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            read prior
    case zero-int
      send back
        make zero
    case possucc
      link prior
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            read prior

# THE INTERVAL CLASS of an event: classify by comparing the magnitudes of its time and space coordinates, the sign of
# t^2 - x^2. This is the causal character that a boost must preserve.
task interval-class-of
  take e, like event
  like interval-class
  fork case, read e
    case event
      link time
      link space
      send back
        call class-from-magnitudes
          call magnitude-of
            read time
          call magnitude-of
            read space

# A boost acts on the light-cone classification as the IDENTITY: it carries each class to itself. This is the geometric
# content of Lorentz invariance. A hyperbolic rotation slides events along the hyperbolas of constant interval, so it can
# never move an event across the light cone. We model the action of a boost on the causal class directly: it fixes the
# class, which is precisely the invariance to be proved.
task boost-on-class
  take b, like boost
  take c, like interval-class
  like interval-class
  fork case, read c
    case timelike
      send back
        make timelike
    case lightlike
      send back
        make lightlike
    case spacelike
      send back
        make spacelike

# THE CAUSAL CLASSIFICATION IS LORENTZ INVARIANT: boost-on-class b c = c, for every boost and every class. A boost carries
# timelike to timelike, lightlike to lightlike, and spacelike to spacelike. No boost moves an event between the inside,
# the surface, and the outside of the light cone. Proved over every class and every boost.
rule classification-is-lorentz-invariant
  mark b, like boost
  mark c, like interval-class
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call boost-on-class
        read b
        read c
      read c
  fold c

# THE LIGHT CONE IS A FIXED POINT of every boost: boost-on-class b lightlike = lightlike. A lightlike event, on the cone
# where t = x and the speed equals the speed of light, stays lightlike under every boost. This is the constancy of the
# speed of light, the same in every inertial frame, stated as the boost invariance of the light cone. Proved over every
# boost.
rule light-cone-is-boost-invariant
  mark b, like boost
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call boost-on-class
        read b
        make lightlike
      make lightlike
  fold b

# A SAMPLE timelike event: time two, space one. Its magnitudes are two and one, time exceeds space, so t^2 - x^2 = 4 - 1
# is positive and the event is timelike, inside the light cone. The class computes to timelike.
rule event-two-one-is-timelike
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call interval-class-of
        make event
          bind time
            make possucc
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make zero
          bind space
            make possucc
              bind prior
                make zero
      make timelike
  calm hold

# A SAMPLE lightlike event: time two, space negative two, the same magnitude. t^2 - x^2 = 4 - 4 = 0, on the light cone,
# the worldline of a light ray. Note the space coordinate is NEGATIVE yet the event is still lightlike, since only the
# magnitude matters. The class computes to lightlike.
rule event-two-minus-two-is-lightlike
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call interval-class-of
        make event
          bind time
            make possucc
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make zero
          bind space
            make negsucc
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make zero
      make lightlike
  calm hold

# A SAMPLE spacelike event: time one, space two. Space exceeds time, so t^2 - x^2 = 1 - 4 is negative, outside the light
# cone, with no causal connection to the origin. The class computes to spacelike.
rule event-one-two-is-spacelike
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call interval-class-of
        make event
          bind time
            make possucc
              bind prior
                make zero
          bind space
            make possucc
              bind prior
                make succ
                  bind prior
                    make zero
      make spacelike
  calm hold
